    "body": "Airboard supports personal and organization workspaces. Your current workspace,\nrole, trial, and entitlement determine which product actions are available.\n\n## Create or join an account\n\nSign in with an enabled identity provider or email magic link. Airboard creates\na personal workspace for a new profile. An invitation can add the same identity\nto another organization without creating a duplicate account.\n\nUse the exact email address that received an invitation. Expired, revoked,\nalready-used, or email-mismatched invitations cannot be accepted.\n\n## Trial activation\n\nThe pilot lasts one month (30 days) after a qualifying first-value event.\nSignup alone does not consume the trial; it starts when you open your first\nboard.\n\n**Plan & Billing**, in the profile menu at the top right, shows when your\npilot runs until. Before you open your first board, it says the pilot has not\nstarted yet.\n\n## When the pilot ends\n\n**Plan & Billing** shows the date your pilot ended. Your saved boards still\nopen and save, and you can still download pictures. New boards, live links and\nAiro voice are off until your pilot is extended.\n\nChoose **Ask for more pilot time** on **Plan & Billing**. The request goes to\nthe Airboard team, who will get back to you. The same button appears when you\ntry to start a new board, and **Share** links to it.\n\n## Paid checkout\n\nPaid checkout is available only when the billing page explicitly shows it as\nenabled. Otherwise displayed prices are proposals, no payment is taken, and the\npage directs you to the managed evaluation path.\n\nWhen checkout is enabled, Stripe handles payment details. Airboard stores the\nbilling references and entitlement state needed to provide access.\n\n## Workspace roles\n\nOwners and administrators manage the workspace in **Settings**. Billing\naccess, member access, and viewer capabilities depend on assigned roles and\npolicy. When you belong to more than one workspace, switch in **Settings →\nWorkspace**. See [Workspace administration](/help/account/admin-console).",
    "searchText": "Account, trial, and billing Understand account setup, invitations, trial activation, expiry, and gated paid checkout. Airboard supports personal and organization workspaces. Your current workspace, role, trial, and entitlement determine which product actions are available. Create or join an account Sign in with an enabled identity provider or email magic link. Airboard creates a personal workspace for a new profile. An invitation can add the same identity to another organization without creating a duplicate account. Use the exact email address that received an invitation. Expired, revoked, already used, or email mismatched invitations cannot be accepted. Trial activation The pilot lasts one month (30 days) after a qualifying first value event. Signup alone does not consume the trial; it starts when you open your first board. Plan & Billing , in the profile menu at the top right, shows when your pilot runs until. Before you open your first board, it says the pilot has not started yet. When the pilot ends Plan & Billing shows the date your pilot ended. Your saved boards still open and save, and you can still download pictures. New boards, live links and Airo voice are off until your pilot is extended. Choose Ask for more pilot time on Plan & Billing . The request goes to the Airboard team, who will get back to you. The same button appears when you try to start a new board, and Share links to it. Paid checkout Paid checkout is available only when the billing page explicitly shows it as enabled. Otherwise displayed prices are proposals, no payment is taken, and the page directs you to the managed evaluation path. When checkout is enabled, Stripe handles payment details. Airboard stores the billing references and entitlement state needed to provide access. Workspace roles Owners and administrators manage the workspace in Settings . Billing access, member access, and viewer capabilities depend on assigned roles and policy. When you belong to more than one workspace, switch in Settings → Workspace . See Workspace administration."
